    "why": "the same painting as one that is kept (young_caucasian_male2, young_caucasian_female2 and middleage_caucasian_male in turn), painted again only at the upper eyelids and the nostrils: cut and compared on 2026-11-14, the two of each pair differ inside the mask by 0.5, 2.3 and 2.0 levels of 255 on average, nearer than any two faces that are kept (2.6 at the nearest; the middle of all the kept pairs is 13). tools/face_library.py --check holds that no two kept faces are nearer than 2.4. They were kept at first, and the one painting was then twice as likely to be drawn as any other. Of each pair the one kept is the atlas with the lower number in its own file name, not the pack's name for either: young_lightskinned_male_diffuse2.png kept and young_lightskinned_male_diffuse3.png left out, young_lightskinned_female_diffuse2.png and young_lightskinned_female_diffuse3.png, middleage_lightskinned_male_diffuse.png and middleage_lightskinned_male_diffuse2.png (the left-out files' names as the pack was downloaded on 2026-11-14; those files are not kept here). An earlier wording of this row said the pack's order of its files decided it; in the pack's own record the left-out skin comes first in all three pairs"
